<p>Read this section before you spend anything, because it's the one the other review pages don't write. <strong>Don't buy this for a half-acre of wet, matted leaves</strong> — it will frustrate you, you'll return it, and you should have bought the EGO. <strong>Don't buy any handheld expecting hours of runtime</strong> — Consumer Reports' tester puts most of the category at 12 to 15 real minutes; the Wood Ranger's 30-minute rating is the longest claim on this page and we still say: plan your jobs in minutes. And if what you want is a big brand name with a printed CFM figure at a low weight, <strong>the Worx LeafJet at rank 4 is the honest cross-shop</strong> — 3.8 pounds, 410 CFM, around a hundred dollars. It's a good machine. It's also nearly twice the weight, with a third of the return window.</p>

<p>If you've read this far and the jobs in your head are the patio, the driveway, the mower deck, the workshop, the car after a wash — then you're the person this ranking was scored for, and the math is short: $69.99, everything in the box, 90 days to disagree for a full refund.</p>

